  "body": "Closes #1403\nRefs #1388\nClaim: mac/mac-mbp\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (mac/mac-mbp-r1423)\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (mac/mac-mbp-w1403)\n\n### Problem\nOn iPad regular width, a sub-forum chosen in the « Sous-forum » picker shows its name over an empty list: nothing is requested.\n\n### Cause\n`CategoriesSidebarColumn` (`RootSidebarView.swift`, `navigationDestination(item: $navigation.selectedSource)`) builds its `TopicListView` with no `.id(source)`. The picker replaces `selectedSource` while the list is on screen, so SwiftUI keeps the same view and the load `.task` is not run for the new model. The compact `TopicsColumn` has `.id(source)`. Same pattern in the Favoris stack's `openedCategory` destination (`RootTabsView.swift`), where `scope.select` replaces `openedCategory`.\n\n### Change\n`.id(source)` / `.id(category)` on those two `TopicListView`s; nothing in `TopicListView` itself (#1414 replaces its load modifier, no overlap). Messages, Plus (already `.id(entry)`) and Recherche do not swap models in place: unchanged.\n\n### Tests\n`TopicFilterSidebarHostedTests.aSourceChosenInThePickerLoads(chosen:)` (hosted, 1366 pt regular width, through `scope(for:).select`, for a `.forum` and a `.subforum` source; asserts the FakeDataSource received the request). Red before the fix, green after. Also green: TopicFilterListHostedTests, SidebarDetailHostedTests, RegularWidthListStyleTests, RootModelTests, TabReselectHostedTests (iPad Pro 13\" iOS 27.2 simulator, deleted after).\n\nSwiftLint checked by hand: line_length (140), file_length, function body length of the new test, vertical_whitespace, trailing_comma, no tuples.\n\nDevice check: iPad by hand (listed on #893).\n\n\n### Notes after review (Opus, mac/mac-mbp-r1423)\n- `.id(category)` on the Favoris `openedCategory` push (`RootTabsView.swift:196`) changes the compact path on purpose: `scope.select` replaces the category there too. That push is not hosted (#870); the iPhone check (Favoris → open a category → change the sub-forum in the picker) is added to the device checks on #893.\n- `.id(source)` also fixes `showCategoryFromFavorites` (`RootModel.swift:314`) when Catégories already shows another list and the Favoris filter is set.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CEAZJkg4akNJrTQb2i\n\n",
