   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, mac/mac-mbp-r1423, head f3f31491)**: APPROVE\n\nFindings (none blocking):\n\n1. **Low**, `App/SwiftHFR/Root/RootTabsView.swift:196`: the `.id(category)` on the Favoris `openedCategory` push changes the compact path, which #1403's acceptance criterion says stays unchanged, and no test covers it (the `openedCategory` push is not hosted, `TopicFilterListHostedTests.swift:57`, #870). The mechanism is the same as the sidebar's: `scope.select` replaces `openedCategory` under the shown list, both models have the same `wantedFilter`, so `.task(id:)` does not run again. The fix is probably right, but the PR has not shown it was broken. Fix: say in the PR that this hunk deliberately changes the compact Favoris → category → « Sous-forum » path and is unhosted, and list the iPhone check on #893. A hosted test is better if it is cheap.\n2. **Detail**, `App/SwiftHFR/Root/RootSidebarView.swift:234`: `.id(source)` also fixes `RootModel.showCategoryFromFavorites` (`RootModel.swift:314`) when Catégories already shows another list with the Favoris filter already set (same `wantedFilter`, so no reload before this PR). Worth one line in the PR's Cause section.\n\nChecked, no problem found:\n- `.id` resets only the list's view state: `titleVisibility`, `newTopic`, `pagePrompt`, and scroll goes back to the top for the new source. The per-source `TopicListModel` cache keeps the rows.\n- The reader in the detail column is reset by `selectedSource.didSet` (`selectedTopic = nil`, `dropReader()`), which runs with or without the `.id`. Nothing in `TopicListView` uses `onDisappear` (LOT-137).\n- No double load: the old view's task is cancelled and the new view runs its task once.\n- The compact `TopicsColumn` root already had `.id(source)`.\n- The other `navigationDestination(item:)` sites do not replace their item under a shown destination: Plus `plusEntry`, Search `selected`, linked readers, About, Offline, Accounts, smileys.\n- #1414 merges cleanly with this PR (`git merge-tree`), and the two changes work together: `sceneAwareListLoad` keeps its `@State` per view, and the `.id` gives each source a fresh copy.\n\n**Verified**: worktree at f3f31491. iPad Pro 13\" (M5) on iOS 27.2 (fresh simulator, deleted after), `CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO`: `TopicFilterListHostedTests` 18/18 green. Mutation (removed `.id(source)` from `RootSidebarView`): both `aSourceChosenInThePickerLoads` cases red with `requests → [\"forums\", \"topics:13:1\"]`, the right reason. The test goes through `scope(for:).select`, the closure the `Picker`'s binding calls (`ForumScopeBar.swift:33`). SwiftLint strict green in CI. I did not run it locally: the new test is 47 effective lines and no line is over 140. Not run: the compact Favoris path (finding 1).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
